@database AminetBrowser.guide
@node MAIN "Aminet Browser for Beam68 0.2"
Aminet Browser is an independent Beam68 Protocol 1 plugin.
It does not require AmiGet and contains no AmiGet source code.

Type aminet:search tracker and press Enter. Select a package and press
Enter to put its details command in the query field; press Enter again
to load the details. Next/Previous rows work the same way.

Commands:
  aminet:search tracker             Search (2-80 characters).
  aminet:info util/wb/Beam68-0.1.lha  Summary and available actions.
  aminet:get util/wb/Beam68-0.1.lha   Confirm and download.
  aminet:install util/wb/Beam68-0.1.lha
                                    Confirm, download and open archive.
  aminet:help                        Usage.

Read full readmes and page through them using the rows in the details view.
Search results can include multiple architectures. Always check the
readme's Architecture and Requires fields for compatibility with your machine.

Installation preparation opens the downloaded archive with its Workbench
archive handler (workbench.library V44+). It does not extract archives or run package installers itself.
Use your archive tool and follow the package's installer or instructions.
If no handler exists, the archive stays in the download drawer.

Preferences -> Plugins -> Aminet Browser -> Settings selects DOWNLOAD_DIR.
Default: RAM:Beam68Downloads (temporary until reboot). Use a disk drawer
for permanent downloads. Keep enough room for the complete archive.

A download has its own window; close it to cancel. Only one Beam68 Aminet
download can be open at a time. The launcher acknowledges that visible
transfer separately from short search/readme requests. Changing the query
or closing Beam68 does not cancel a confirmed download; use its window.
Completed files appear only after the transfer is checked and renamed.
An interrupted transfer can leave a Beam68Aminetxx/archive.part drawer;
remove it manually when no download is running. Partial files are not installed.

Requires AmigaOS 3.0+, an active bsdsocket.library TCP/IP stack, and optional
Workbench archive tools for installation. No AmiGet dependency or shell command
interpolation. Uses classic HTTP (unencrypted) to the fixed Aminet host, not TLS.
Packages have no authenticity guarantee from the transport; review them before
running their installers. Live previews are disabled; networking starts on Enter.
Search/readme responses are limited to 256 KB and 20 seconds, downloads to
64 MB and five minutes. Resolver timeouts are controlled by your TCP/IP stack.
The HTML parser follows Aminet's current layout and reports unsupported pages.

Aminet: https://aminet.net
This plugin is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Aminet operators.
Archive downloads require a declared size and must match it before commit.
Installation preparation also checks the archive signature before opening it.
@endnode
